ent\\\": \\\"sizeof\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"static\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"string\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"switch\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"throw\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"try\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"typeof\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"ulong\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"unsafe\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"using\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"virtual\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"volatile\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong>Contextual keywords</strogn>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"add\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"ascending\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"dynamic\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"into\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"global\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"group \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"join\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"let\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "identifier "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a name that determines a specific object or a specific class of objects "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Also, you have identifiers for class, function, variables, etc."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n5le03ob04aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "theory "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a set of statements that explain a determined matter "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I used to try to remember the theory; I didn't realize that you learn easier when practicing."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n5le03ob04aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "collection "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "group, accumulation or selection"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Functions are a collection of statements that perform a specific task."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n5le03ob04aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "treat "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to deal with something in a certain way "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It is an object-oriented language because it's able to treat each class as an object instead of taking it as separate data and code."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n5le03ob04aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "repeatedly "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "happening once and again"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Okay, one mistake that I would make repeatedly was to name the variables with the names of a function."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n5le03ob04aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "In the web, find different examples of C# programming. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read and analyze the syntax of each example. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "In a poster, write the ones you consider are easy to replicate."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Show your poster to a partner. Describe each text highlighting keywords, initial statement, variables, class and functions."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I find more information about C# programming."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make comparisons between texts. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I describe texts written In C# programming with their respective syntax."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe7n5le03ob04re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<strong>Jeremy</strong>: Why is C# an object-oriented language? </br>\n<strong>Lily</strong>: It is an object-oriented language because it's able to treat each class as an object instead of taking it as separate data and code. </br>\n<strong>Jeremy</strong>: What exactly is a class? </br>\n<strong>Lily</strong>: A class is a data structure that encompasses a set of data and behaviors; it's like a blueprint. </br>\n<strong>Jeremy</strong>: How do I start my C# program? </br>\n<strong>Lily</strong>: The first statement is \"using System.\" Here you include the namespaces in the program. In the past, I would start by writing it into the code, but now, the program that I use writes this first part automatically. </br>"}, {"time": "42000", "image": "enpe7n5le03ob04re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<strong>Jeremy</strong>: What about the keywords? </br>\n<strong>Lily</strong>: There are keywords for different functions. For example, \u201cbool,\u201d which introduces a Boolean logic of true and false. Another keyword is \"if,\" which determines a condition that can take place inside classes. Also, you have identifiers for class, function, variables, etc. </br>\n<strong>Jeremy</strong>: This is very specific information and difficult to understand. </br>\n<strong>Lily</strong>: Don't worry! I also used to think that, but programming is about practice. Some months ago, I would spend a lot of time to practice programming at home. More than understanding what a variable is, you should remember the identifier used when writing a variable; it cannot have any spaces, start with a number or an underscore, or have any other symbols. When I started programming, I used to try to remember the theory; I didn't realize that you learn easier when practicing."}, {"time": "106600", "image": "enpe7n5le03ob04re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<strong>Jeremy</strong>: Okay, one mistake that I would make repeatedly was to name the variables with the names of a function. </br>\n<strong>Lily</strong>: That's something very important to take into account. Functions are a collection of statements that perform a specific task. If you give your variable the same name as a function, the computer doesn't know if it has to perform an action or not. On the other hand, a variable is a data member of a class used for storing data."}], "coverimg": "enpe7n5le03ob04re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n5le03ob04re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about C# as an object oriented programming language."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can discuss and use basic syntax in C#."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can identify and use C# keywords."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What are the most common commands in C#? "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What could happen if you mistype a word in C#?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name",